WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.725
It's a loop of five steps.

2
00:00:01.725 --> 00:00:06.868
A rule tests actual state against the
record, a difference becomes a typed finding,

3
00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:11.028
the finding becomes a task with an
owner and a clock, the change runs

4
00:00:11.028 --> 00:00:15.112
on the platform's own surface, and
a re-read closes it with evidence.

5
00:00:15.112 --> 00:00:18.660
The important part is what the
coordination layer doesn't do:

6
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.576
it never makes the change itself.

7
00:00:20.576 --> 00:00:25.038
Its job is to make every drift
owned, clocked, approved and proven.

8
00:00:25.038 --> 00:00:28.744
Federal policy is heading the
same way for cloud providers,

9
00:00:28.744 --> 00:00:32.450
and the program applies that
logic to an agency's own estate.

10
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.660
Inside that loop, every
request runs a chain.
